# Acme Platform SLA Commitments
**Document type:** Customer-facing SLA
**Classification:** Internal (governs external commitments)
**Effective:** January 1, 2026
**Version:** 3.0

---

## Service Level Agreement — Platform Services

This document defines Acme Corp's service level commitments to customers by service tier.

---

## Tier Definitions

| Tier | Description | Customers |
|------|-------------|-----------|
| Enterprise | Dedicated SLA with contractual penalties | Signed enterprise contracts |
| Business | Standard SLA with credits | Self-serve business plans |
| Starter | Best-effort, no contractual SLA | Starter and free plans |

---

## Uptime Commitments

| Service | Enterprise SLA | Business SLA | Measurement Period |
|---------|---------------|-------------|-------------------|
| API Gateway | 99.9% | 99.5% | Monthly |
| Core API (CRUD) | 99.9% | 99.5% | Monthly |
| File Ingestion | 99.5% | 99.0% | Monthly |
| Wiki Services | 99.5% | 99.0% | Monthly |
| Authentication | 99.99% | 99.9% | Monthly |

---

## Response Time Commitments

| Service | P50 Target | P99 Target | Tier |
|---------|-----------|-----------|------|
| API read operations | 200ms | 1.5s | Enterprise |
| API write operations | 500ms | 3.0s | Enterprise |
| File ingest (start) | 1s | 5s | Enterprise |
| Wiki query | 300ms | 2.0s | Enterprise |

---

## Incident Response Times (Enterprise)

| Severity | Response Time | Resolution Target | Communication Frequency |
|----------|--------------|-------------------|------------------------|
| P1 (>5% error rate or >5min downtime) | 15 minutes | 4 hours | Every 30 minutes |
| P2 (degraded performance, <5% errors) | 1 hour | 8 hours | Every 2 hours |
| P3 (minor issue, workaround available) | 4 hours | 3 business days | On resolution |

---

## Service Credits (Enterprise)

| Monthly Uptime | Credit Applied |
|---------------|---------------|
| 99.0% – 99.9% | 10% of monthly fee |
| 95.0% – 99.0% | 25% of monthly fee |
| Below 95.0%   | 50% of monthly fee |

Credits are applied to the next billing cycle. Credits are the sole remedy for SLA breaches under this agreement.

---

## Exclusions

SLA commitments do not apply during:
- Scheduled maintenance windows (communicated 48 hours in advance)
- Force majeure events
- Customer-caused incidents
- Incidents in third-party services outside Acme's control

---

## Planned Maintenance Windows

Scheduled maintenance: Sundays 02:00–04:00 UTC. Customers are notified via status page and email at least 48 hours in advance.

---

## SLA Monitoring and Reporting

- Real-time status page: status.acme-corp.example
- Monthly uptime reports available in customer dashboard
- Enterprise customers receive monthly SLA compliance reports via email
